            <ArticleTitle>[Burkitt's lymphoma presenting as ovarian tumor].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>282-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">MagyOnkol.2012.56.4.282</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Burkitt's lymphoma is a rapidly progressing tumor, which could be cured in 60-80% of cases. Its infiltration of the ileo-cecal region often spreads to the ovaries, though primary ovarian manifestation is also common. By presenting our case of a 27-year-old nulliparous patient with primary ovarian Burkitt's lymphoma, we would like to draw attention to its diagnostic and therapeutic difficulties.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
